{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '490,535p' src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc; sed -n '780,880p' src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc; sed -n '1520,1690p' test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc; sed -n '305,339p' docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md; cat collab/1791236272936-architect-h2-contract-r3.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log; tail -90 collab/1791236352519-stream-engineer-head-h2-r4.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '490,535p' src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc; sed -n '780,880p' src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc; sed -n '1520,1690p' test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc; sed -n '305,339p' docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md; cat collab/1791236272936-architect-h2-contract-r3.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log; tail -90 collab/1791236352519-stream-engineer-head-h2-r4.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- absorb!\n  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n   id is outstanding and whose identity is the outstanding entry's\n   reflection's own identity is taken: a not-found error marks the\n   reflection gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's\n   descriptor and declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is\n   emitted on the event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is\n   filed under its id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose\n   id is not outstanding, answers whose identity is not the\n   reflection's own -- a mismatch never completes a request, which\n   stays outstanding, and an answer that carries no identity\n   completes no identity request -- and values that are not\n   well-formed answers,\n   are dropped as diagnostics. The answer to a named request is the\n   resolve's (absorb-named!).\"\n  [link v]\n  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n        (if (named? (:req entry))\n          (absorb-named! link id entry v)\n          (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n                req (:req entry)\n                op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n                e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n            (when (and (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n                       (= (:dao.stream/identity v) (:identity @refl)))\n              (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n              (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n              (cond\n                (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n                (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n                    (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n                              (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n                      (emit! link v)))\n\n                (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n                ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n                ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n                (when (nil? e)\n                  (learn! refl v)\n                  (emit! link v))\n\n                (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n                (emit! link v)\n\n          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)))\n      (swap! refl assoc :closed? true :ids #{}))\n    (result :dao.stream/ok)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The link's resolve (2.4)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- named-id\n  \"The least id in `entries` -- the link's outstanding or filed map --\n   whose request is a named request for the name `n`, if any.\"\n  [entries n]\n  (first\n    (sort\n      (keep (fn [[id e]]\n              (let [r (:req e)]\n                (when (and (named? r) (= n (:dao.stream.remote/name r)))\n                  id)))\n            entries))))\n\n\n(defn- send-named!\n  \"Append one named descriptor request for `n` to the channel writer,\n   outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a refused send\n   leaves the request unsent and the next resolve sends again. The\n   request carries the name in place of :dao.stream/identity.\"\n  [link n]\n  (let [req {:dao.stream.remote/name n\n             :dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/descriptor\n             :dao.stream.remote/args []\n             :dao.stream.remote/id (mint-id! link)}\n        r (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)]\n    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n      (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n             {:req req :asks 0 :reflection nil}))\n    r))\n\n\n(defn- resolved\n  \"The outcome a filed answer to a named request yields: ok with the\n   remote descriptor of the stream the name mapped to -- its own\n   identity, over this link's channel -- and the entry's declared\n   surface; a protocol error translated per the reflection's rules,\n   not-found included; any other outcome the source's own map.\"\n  [link ans]\n  (cond\n    (some? (:dao.stream.remote/error ans))\n    (translated (:dao.stream.remote/error ans))\n\n    (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome ans))\n    (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity ans)]\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n       :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n                               :dao.stream/identity identity\n                               :dao.stream/channel (:channel @link)}\n       :dao.stream/identity identity\n       :dao.stream.remote/surface (:dao.stream.remote/surface ans)})\n\n    :else\n    (dissoc (bare-outcome ans)\n            :dao.stream.remote/name :dao.stream.remote/surface)))\n\n\n(defn- resolve-name\n  \"The link's resolve: drain, then a filed answer for the name is\n   returned and forgotten -- a name is looked up afresh each time it\n   is asked, never remembered. Otherwise a named descriptor request is\n   sent if none is outstanding, and the answer is transport-error with\n   :dao.stream/retry? true, as cursor answers. A send the writer\n   refuses with full is retried by the next resolve; any other refusal\n   is the writer's own outcome, leaves nothing outstanding and is\n   remembered nowhere -- the writer is the source of truth for what it\n   can carry -- so each resolve of that name attempts the send again.\n   After channel loss the answer is transport-error naming\n   channel-gone, not retryable.\"\n  [link n]\n  (drain! link)\n  (if-some [id (named-id (:filed @link) n)]\n    (let [ans (:ans (get (:filed @link) id))]\n      (swap! link update :filed dissoc id)\n      (resolved link ans))\n    (cond\n      (:channel-gone? @link)\n      (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)\n\n      :else\n      (if-some [id (named-id (:outstanding @link) n)]\n        (do (count-ask! link id) (retry-read))\n        (let [r (send-named! link n)]\n          (if (contains? #{:dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/full}\n                         (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n            (retry-read)\n            r))))))\n\n\n(deftype ReflectionHandle\n  [state]\n\n  stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n\n\n\n(defn- link-of\n  \"The link `ls` keeps for the toy's channel, read through a reflection\n   attached on it: the link state is the reflection's :link.\"\n  [ls t]\n  (:link @(.-state (:dao.stream/handle\n                      ((:attach ls) {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n                                     :dao.stream/identity \"probe\"\n                                     :dao.stream/channel (:channel t)})))))\n\n\n(defn- refusing-links\n  [t attempts outcome]\n  (remote/links {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n                 {(:channel t)\n                  {:reader (:ba t)\n                   :writer (counting-writer attempts outcome)}}}))\n\n\n(deftest an-uncarryable-name-is-a-terminal-resolve\n  (doseq [outcome [:dao.stream/invalid-value :dao.stream/closed]]\n    (testing (str outcome)\n      (let [t (toy)\n            attempts (atom 0)\n            ls (refusing-links t attempts outcome)\n            link (link-of ls t)\n            _ (reset! attempts 0)\n            resolve #((:resolve ls) (:channel t) \"yin.head/p\")]\n        (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome outcome} (resolve)))\n        (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome outcome} (resolve))\n            \"terminal, and the writer asked again\")\n        (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome outcome} (resolve)))\n        (is (= 3 @attempts) \"each resolve attempts the send\")\n        (is (= {} (:outstanding @link)))\n        (is (= {} (:filed @link))))))\n  (testing \"a hundred refused names: the link holds none of them\"\n    (let [t (toy)\n          attempts (atom 0)\n          ls (refusing-links t attempts :dao.stream/invalid-value)\n          link (link-of ls t)\n          names (set (map #(str \"yin.head/n\" %) (range 100)))]\n      (doseq [n names]\n        (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value}\n               ((:resolve ls) (:channel t) n))))\n      (is (= {} (:outstanding @link)))\n      (is (= {} (:filed @link)))\n      (is (not-any? names (tree-seq coll? seq @link))\n          \"no name in any key of the link\")))\n  (testing \"full is backpressure: retried by the next resolve\"\n    (let [s (ring 1)\n          t (toy)\n          id (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor s))\n          peer (served-peer {id (entry s #{:reader})} t)\n          ls (remote/links {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n                            {(:channel t)\n                             {:reader (:ba t)\n                              :writer (full-then-forward-writer (:ab t) 1)}}})\n          resolve #((:resolve ls) (:channel t) \"yin.head/p\")]\n      (is (= retry (resolve)))\n      (is (= 0 (count (op-requests (:ab t) :dao.stream/descriptor))))\n      (is (= retry (resolve)))\n      (is (= 1 (count (op-requests (:ab t) :dao.stream/descriptor))))\n      (serve-named! peer {\"yin.head/p\" id})\n      (is (= id (:dao.stream/identity (resolve)))))))\n\n\n(deftest an-answer-with-no-identity-completes-no-identity-request\n  (doseq [e [:dao.stream.remote/not-found :dao.stream.remote/oversize]]\n    (testing (str \"absent identity, \" e)\n      (let [t (toy)\n            r (:dao.stream/handle (attach (:a-end t) nil {}))\n            link (:link @(.-state r))]\n        (is (contains? (:outstanding @link) 0) \"the probe is outstanding\")\n        (stream/append! (:ba t) {:dao.stream.remote/id 0\n                                 :dao.stream.remote/name \"unasked\"\n                                 :dao.stream.remote/error e})\n        (is (= retry (stream/cursor r :dao.stream/oldest))\n            \"dropped: the reflection is not gone\")\n        (is (contains? (:outstanding @link) 0) \"the probe stays outstanding\"))))\n  (testing \"an explicit nil identity behaves as before\"\n    (let [t (toy)\n          r (:dao.stream/handle (attach (:a-end t) nil {}))\n          link (:link @(.-state r))]\n      (stream/append! (:ba t) {:dao.stream.remote/id 0\n                               :dao.stream/identity nil\n                               :dao.stream.remote/error\n                               :dao.stream.remote/not-found})\n      (is (= {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n              :dao.stream.remote/reason :dao.stream.remote/not-found}\n             (stream/cursor r :dao.stream/oldest))\n          \"it matches the nil identity and marks the reflection gone\")\n      (is (not (contains? (:outstanding @link) 0))))))\n**Channel loss.** A channel ends when its reader answers `end`: the\nprojection closed it (3.1), the pair adapter closed it on an `in` gap or\nend (3.3), or the medium is gone. The link then abandons its outstanding\nids and reports each\nabandoned `append!` on the event writer as `append-unknown` (2.5), and\nanswers later `cursor` and `next` `transport-error` with\n`:dao.stream.remote/reason :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone`, not retryable;\n`append!` keeps answering the channel writer's own outcome, `closed` once\nthe channel is down. Filed answers are still returned. Reattachment is the\ncaller's policy, by `attach!` on the same descriptor.\n\n**Resolve.** A link also answers `resolve` `name`, for no reflection. It\ndrains, then returns and forgets a filed answer for the name: `ok` with\nthe remote descriptor of the identity answered over the link's channel,\n`:dao.stream/identity` and `:dao.stream.remote/surface`; or the filed\n`not-found` as `transport-error` with\n`:dao.stream.remote/reason :dao.stream.remote/not-found`, which marks\nnothing. A filed `oversize` is returned the same way, with its own name as\nthe reason. Otherwise it sends the named request if none is outstanding for\nthe name and answers `transport-error` with `:dao.stream/retry? true`, as\n`cursor` does. A send the channel writer refuses with `full` is retried by\nthe next `resolve`; any other refusal is returned as the writer's own\noutcome, leaves nothing outstanding and is remembered nowhere, so each\n`resolve` of that name attempts the send again. A named answer is filed\nonly when its id is outstanding and it echoes the name asked. An answer\nthat carries no `:dao.stream/identity` completes no identity request.\nAfter channel loss `resolve` answers `transport-error` with\n`:dao.stream.remote/reason :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone`. On a channel\ndescriptor this peer holds no channel for, `resolve` answers `not-found`,\nas `attach!` does. The caller attaches the descriptor answered with\n`attach!`; from there nothing in this section changes.\n\n**Refused.** A filed `:dao.stream/refused` is returned verbatim for the\noperation it answers and marks nothing: refusal is per operation\n(`dao.stream.md`, Result Convention).\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-05 21:38:33 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-06 04:38:33 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: f56f11bb-ea1a-422e-8dc5-dd66b6ff7938\n\n## Finding 1: (b), drop the memory entirely\n\nThe reviewer's citation holds: `remote.cljc:876` stores the whole refused name per link with no bound. I signed that sentence in round 2 and called the memory sound; it was correct but not bounded, and it is not needed.\n\n**Reasoning**\n- **Derive, don't persist decides it.** The channel writer is the source of truth for whether a value can be carried. Asking it again re-derives the same refusal, so the link has nothing to remember.\n- **No hidden state, bounded below `dao.stream`.** With (b) a `resolve` of an unsendable name leaves the link exactly as it found it, apart from the id counter. Option (a) adds two bounds, an eviction rule and a beyond-the-bound answer to a contract that needs none of them.\n- **The original finding stays closed.** Its defect was that `resolve` answered retry forever for a name that could never be sent. Under (b) every call returns the writer's refusal as terminal data, and no id is left outstanding. Each call still mints an id and costs one refused append. That is a counter and a constant, the caller's own loop pays for it, and nothing grows.\n- **`closed` needs no memory either.** A closed writer keeps answering `closed`, and after the reader ends the link answers `channel-gone`.\n\n**Exact replacement for 2.4** (`dao.stream.remote.md:325-329`, replacing from \"A send the channel writer refuses\" through \"until channel loss.\"):\n\n> A send the channel writer refuses with `full` is retried by the next `resolve`; any other refusal is returned as the writer's own outcome, leaves nothing outstanding and is remembered nowhere, so each `resolve` of that name attempts the send again.\n\n**Code:** remove `:unsendable` (`remote.cljc:862-863`, `:874-876`); the `:else r` branch then covers every refusal other than `full`. Update the `resolve-name` docstring to match.\n\n**Tests**\n- Rework `an-uncarryable-name-is-a-terminal-resolve`: for `invalid-value` and for `closed`, three calls give the same writer outcome, three sends are attempted, and `:outstanding` and `:filed` stay empty.\n- Add a many-name case: resolving 100 distinct refused names leaves the link holding none of them (no name in `:outstanding`, `:filed` or any other key).\n- Keep the `full` case as it is.\n\n## Finding 2: the fix is right and sufficient\n\nThe citation holds: `remote.cljc:93-97` now admits a named error with no identity, and `remote.cljc:513` compares a missing identity as `nil`.\n\n- **Fix:** in the identity branch of `absorb!`, require `(contains? v :dao.stream/identity)` before the equality at `:513`. That restores the pre-H2 behaviour exactly for identity requests, since the old validator required the key for every answer.\n- **Sufficient:** the named branch is unaffected, because `absorb-named!` requires the echoed name (`remote.cljc:482-484`). An answer with a matching identity and a stray name is still accepted, as an open map allows.\n- **Tests:** as the reviewer says, for a `nil`-identity reflection, an absent identity is dropped and the probe stays outstanding, for both `not-found` and `oversize`; an explicit `nil` identity is tested separately.\n\n**Contract sentence: yes, one, in 2.4 Resolve.** Insert after \"it echoes the name asked.\":\n\n> An answer that carries no `:dao.stream/identity` completes no identity request.\n\n**`nil` identity for a reflection:** a pre-existing gap, outside H2. `valid-remote-descriptor?` (`remote.cljc:927-929`) defers to the generic `stream/valid-descriptor?`. I did not open that function; that it admits `nil` is the reviewer's reproduction. Whether a `nil` identity should be legal is a `dao.stream.md` question. Do not expand the slice; record it as a follow-up.\n\n## The test race: H2 does not carry it\n\n- The find-then-bind window is in the test only (`head_ws_test.cljc:708-713`), not in `serve`.\n- It became necessary because of the ruling-4 fix, and the window is microseconds on loopback.\n- A retry loop would also have to handle a bind that fails asynchronously through the lifecycle medium, which is more test machinery than the risk warrants.\n- If the lane ever flakes on address-in-use, add a bounded retry then.\n\n**Sign-off:** the contract text is signed off once the finding-1 replacement and the finding-2 sentence are in as written above. No further Architect round is needed if they go in verbatim.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-05 21:41:49 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-06 04:41:49 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: 820fb1cc-b82c-4ee6-96c7-7a170107243d\n\n# head-h2 round 4 report\n\nBoth rulings are applied and the 21-namespace JVM run passes: 302 tests, 2985 assertions, 0 failures. I checked the item-2 citation before changing anything, and it holds. `dao.stream/valid-descriptor?` only requires the identity *key* to be present, so a descriptor with `{:dao.stream/identity nil}` attaches. The identity branch of `absorb!` then compared a missing identity (`nil`) with the reflection's `nil`, so an answer with no identity could consume that reflection's probe.\n\n## 1. The unsendable memory is gone\n\n**Code (`remote.cljc`):**\n- `:unsendable` is removed; `grep` finds no occurrence left.\n- In `resolve-name`, `ok` and `full` still answer retry. Every other refusal returns the writer's own outcome, leaves nothing outstanding and is remembered nowhere.\n- The `resolve-name` docstring now says the same.\n\n**Contract (`dao.stream.remote.md` 2.4):** the old text, from \"A send the channel writer refuses\" through \"until channel loss.\", is replaced with the sentence verbatim. The paragraph is rewrapped.\n\n**Tests (`remote_test.cljc`):**\n- `an-uncarryable-name-is-a-terminal-resolve` is the one test reworked, as instructed.\n  - For `invalid-value` and for `closed`, three calls give the same writer outcome and **three** sends are attempted.\n  - `:outstanding` and `:filed` stay `{}`.\n  - A new case resolves 100 distinct refused names. Afterwards `:outstanding` and `:filed` are `{}`, and no name appears anywhere in the link's value (checked with `tree-seq` over the whole link map).\n  - The `full` case is unchanged.\n- The tests reach the link through a reflection attached on the same `links`, via its `:link`. That needed no new API. I left the field access without a type hint so ClojureDart has nothing to resolve.\n\n## 2. An answer with no identity completes no identity request\n\n**Code:** the identity branch of `absorb!` now requires `(contains? v :dao.stream/identity)` before comparing. The `absorb!` docstring says so. The named branch is untouched.\n\n**Contract:** the sentence is inserted verbatim after \"it echoes the name asked.\"\n\n**Tests:** `an-answer-with-no-identity-completes-no-identity-request`.\n- For a reflection with a `nil` identity, an answer with no identity key is dropped, the reflection is not gone (`cursor` answers retry), and probe id 0 stays outstanding. This holds for both `not-found` and `oversize`.\n- A separate case covers an explicit `nil` identity. It still matches as before H2, and `not-found` marks the reflection gone.\n- Without the fix, the absent-identity `not-found` case would mark the reflection gone, and the `oversize` case would consume the probe.\n\n## Commands and outcomes (foreground)\n- **The 21-namespace combined run** (the same command as rounds 2 and 3) gave **302 tests, 2985 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n- **`clj -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test`:** 33 tests, 337 assertions, 0 failures.\n- **`clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc`:** 0 errors. There is 1 warning, the unused `peer2` at `remote_test.cljc:661`, which predates H2.\n- **`dao.stream.remote.md`:** no line over 80 columns and no non-ASCII character. Both new sentences are present verbatim, at lines 325-328 and 330.\n\n## Unresolved\n- **Follow-up, outside H2 and unchanged:** whether a reflection may have a `nil` identity at all. `valid-descriptor?` accepts `{:dao.stream/identity nil}` today, and the explicit-`nil` test documents the behaviour as it stands.\n- Node and Dart lanes were not run, per the brief.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"clj -M - <<'CLJ'\n(require '[dao.stream :as s] '[dao.stream.remote :as r] '[dao.stream.ringbuffer :as rb])\n(defn ring [] (:dao.stream/handle (rb/create\"'! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity 64})))\n(doseq [err [:dao.stream.remote/not-found :dao.stream.remote/oversize]]\n  (let [ab (ring) ba (ring) cd {:dao.stream/type :review/channel :dao.stream/identity \"c\"}\n        ls (r/links {:dao.stream.remote/channels {cd {:reader ba :writer ab}}})\n        h (:dao.stream/handle ((:attach ls) {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote :dao.stream/identity nil :dao.stream/channel cd}))\n        link (:link @(.-state h))]\n    (s/append! ba {:dao.stream.remote/id 0 :dao.stream.remote/name \"unasked\" :dao.stream.remote/error err})\n    (prn {:error err :cursor-outcome (s/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest) :probe-still-outstanding (contains? (:outstanding @link) 0)})))\n(doseq [outcome [:dao.stream/invalid-value :dao.stream/closed]]\n  (let [attempts (atom 0)\n        writer (reify s/IDaoStreamWriter (append! [_ _] (swap! attempts inc) {:dao.stream/outcome outcome}))\n        link ((ns-resolve '\"'dao.stream.remote 'new-link) {} {:reader (ring) :writer writer} {})\n        initial @link\n        resolve-name (ns-resolve 'dao.stream.remote 'resolve-name)\n        results (doall (for [i (range 100)] (resolve-name link (str i (apply str (repeat 10000 \\\"x\\\"))))))]\n    (prn {:refusal outcome :all-terminal (every? #(= {:dao.stream/outcome outcome} %) results)\n          :attempts @attempts :next-id (:next-id @link)\n          :state-unchanged-except-id (= (dissoc initial :next-id) (dissoc @link :next-id))})))\nCLJ\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
